        "baud_rate": 57600,
        "comments": "-> [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]] general information about the serial port, serial port cable, etc.\n\n{{media:zyxel:lte5398-m904:console-header.jpeg?400|Serial console header location}}\n\nSerial console pins headers are absent and the pin holes are filled with solder. It's possible to make it work by pushing pin headers against those solder contacts with one hand and typing with the other, which is far from easy but it's doable if one doesn't want to solder and doesn't need to use the console a lot. \n\nPinout:\n     [o] GND\n     [ ] key - no pin\n     [o] RX\n     [o] TX\n     [o] 3.3V Vcc\n\n3.3V should **not** be connected to USB TTL UART adapters, as per [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial]].\n\n^ Serial connection parameters\\\\ for ZyXEL LTE5398-M904 | 57600, 8N1, 3.3V |\n",
